course: dictionary
lesson: 487
title: Ascender
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An ascender is the part of a lowercase letter that reaches up above the middle of the line. «Tall parts of letters (b, d, h) are ascenders.» Letters like b, d, f, h, k, l and t all have one.
explain: Small letters like a, c and e sit between the lines. The line the letters sit on is the baseline. «Tall ones like b, d, h reach up» above the small letters, so you can spot an ascender by checking whether a letter stretches higher than a, c or e.
explain: The word has other meanings too. In climbing, an ascender is a tool that grips a rope so a climber can go up it. It can also mean a person or thing that goes up. In handwriting and printing, though, it is always about the tall parts of letters.
fact: An ascender is the tall part of a lowercase letter that goes up above the middle of the line.
fact: Lowercase letters with ascenders are b, d, f, h, k, l and t.
fact: «Tall letters with ascenders» are used in handwriting lessons.
fact: A descender is the tail that goes down below the line, as in g, j, p, q and y.
fact: The line the letters sit on is called the baseline.
exercise: Which of these letters has an ascender? | e | *d | c | a
exercise: What is the name for the tail that goes below the line, as in g, p and y? | Baseline | Ascender | *Descender | Climbing tool
exercise: Which of these is a climbing tool that grips a rope so a climber can go up it? | Descender | Baseline | Lowercase letter | *Ascender
test: In handwriting, what is the name of the line that letters sit on? | Ascender | *Baseline | Descender | Tail
test: Which letter has a tail that hangs below the line? | *y | d | l | t
exam: Which sentence correctly describes an ascender? | An ascender is the line that the letters sit on | *An ascender is the tall part of a letter, as in b, d or h, that reaches up above the middle of the line | An ascender is a letter that sits between the lines, like a, c and e | An ascender is the tail that hangs below the line, as in g
